[Music]  the NHS is close to crisis this  Christmas a combination of seasonal  strained and staff on strike and now  more action confirmed by nurses  including Carmel O'Boyle who says it's  an agonizing decision I have colleagues  who are using food banks and because  they can't afford to feed their families  and that has again a knock-on effect  onto patient care you can't expect  somebody to be looking after you know  someone else if you can't look after  your own it's really difficult nurses  want the Prime Minister sat down for  talks they say salaries aren't enough to  deliver the care patients need  with the Prime Minister visiting a  charity won't move on pay I'm really sad  and disappointed about the disruption  that has been caused to so many people's  lives particularly at Christmas time you  know when it comes to it was a difficult  question of setting public sector pay  the government has acted fairly  unreasonably in accepting all the  recommendations of the public sector pay  review bodies that's an independent  process the government has listened to  but nurses say the reviews he talks of  were inadequate and tens of thousands  will walk out again so after the strikes  that happened last week the government  still continues ignoring what nurses are  saying and and therefore we feel we've  got no choice than to take action again  in January to try and again send a very  strong signal to the government that  unless they come back to the table this  will need to continue the NHS has never  faced such industrial action nurses went  on strike on the 15th and 20th of  December while ambulance workers walked  out on the 21st and it continues in the  new year with nursing strikes on the  18th and 19th of January and more  ambulance staff action on the 11th and  23rd nurses in school Scotland will also  strike in the new year  the problem is this is the busiest  period for the NHS services and staff  are under immense pressure with the  triple challenge of flu covered and  other viruses  the industrial action is disruptive and  in deadlock leaving uncertainty for  patients and a winter of discomfort for  the Health Service Laura bundock Sky  News

